{
  "_note": "ENCOUNTERS — the P11 format, shaped by slice ruling 4 (2026-08-23): combat is simulated and toggleable, so an encounter collapses to a difficulty-ranked row with an enemy list. The full scripted form exists ONLY for the prologue battles, which are fixed by design and precede the map. Authored 2026-08-25 from ENEMY-REVIEW.md. FORMAT IS PROPOSED, NOT RULED — this is the sketch for review.",
  "format": {
    "sliceRow": "id · difficulty (an integer rank the battle list is sorted by) · enemies (unit ids with counts) · powerSources (optional: the battle's external pool and any scheduled gains) · terrainHint (optional). Nothing else — ruling 4 means no maps, no scripting for slice battles.",
    "prologueBattle": "The five fixed battles carry the full shape: setup (placed units by zone), schedule (phase-keyed spawns by edge), loseAfter, retreat, civilians, events. CLOCK RULING 2026-08-23: schedules count PHASES — the word turn never appears in encounter data. Placement is by hex — see format.placement.",
    "powerSources": "kind: external (pool at battle start) | arrival (one-time +X when a unit enters, stays in the pool after its death) | clock (per-phase or conditional gains live on the unit rows themselves — the Lieutenant's EOT, the Vampire Lord's kills).",
    "placement": "HEX PLACEMENT, ruled 2026-08-25 (zones were vagueries): at:{col,row} places on that hex; at:{near:{col,row},range:N} deploys anywhere within N of it; at:{oneOf:[{col,row},...]} is a scripted either/or. Board: the engine’s 12×12 odd-r grid (engine/src/core/hex.ts), row 0 = enemy edge, row 11 = player edge. The old zone word is kept as `was` for provenance; the hex is authoritative. Multi-unit entries list one hex per unit in `hexes`."
  },
